# Per-profile website blocking configuration
#
# Format (with groups):
#   profile_name|group_name|domain1,domain2,domain3
#
# Format (without groups, backward compatible):
#   profile_name|domain1,domain2,domain3
#   (uses the "default" group)
#
# Groups let you have different domain lists for different time periods:
#   website-blocking.sh enable alice after_school
#   website-blocking.sh enable alice evening
#
# Profile names must match those in /etc/config/parental_profiles.
# MACs are read from parental_profiles, not from this file.

# Alice: different blocks at different times
alice|after_school|youtube.com,www.youtube.com,tiktok.com,www.tiktok.com
alice|evening|youtube.com,www.youtube.com,tiktok.com,www.tiktok.com,netflix.com,www.netflix.com,disneyplus.com,www.disneyplus.com

# Bob: same blocks all day (uses default group)
bob|tiktok.com,www.tiktok.com,snapchat.com,www.snapchat.com

# Teen: block Reddit during study time
teen|study_time|reddit.com,www.reddit.com